{
  "verdict": "request",
  "cause": "IMAGE_FIELD_IGNORED",
  "fix": {"action": "change_request_format", "target": "messages[0].content", "value": "Make content an array of parts: [{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"What is in this picture? Describe it in two sentences.\"},{\"type\":\"image_url\",\"image_url\":{\"url\":\"data:image/png;base64,<BASE64>\"}}] and remove the non-standard 'images' field"}
  "rationale": "The request puts the PNG in a top-level 'images' array on the message, which is an Ollama-style field. llama-server's /v1/chat/completions reads images only from 'image_url' content parts, so it ignores 'images'. The usage confirms this: prompt_tokens is 21 for a short text prompt, with no image tokens added. The mmproj is passed on the launch command, so the projector is loaded and the reply asking for a picture is the model correctly reacting to a prompt with no image."
}
